  "body": "The Wire Contour has a compensation mode since #4134: `computer` (the default), `control` and `wear`. The mode is in the project file and in MCP (`compensation` in `add_operation` and `edit_operation`).\n\nThe wire page in the UI does not show the mode. A user of the GUI cannot set it.\n\nWork:\n\n1. Add a \"Compensation\" choice (Computer, Control, Wear) to the wire page (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/wire_page.rs`). The edit goes through `EditOperationParams`, as each other wire field does.\n2. Show the command door's refusal when the mode is not computer and the cut has an open run, a taper, a 4-axis cut, a burnout, tabs, the arc lead or an exit pick.\n3. Add the behaviour test and update the page's layout test (`layout_page_*`).\n\nDone means: a user sets the mode on the wire page, undo restores the previous mode, and the LN2W post writes `G41` / `G42 Hnnn` for the cut.\n\nRefs #4134. Two open PRs change `wire_page.rs` now (#4221, #4232). Start after they merge.\n",
